comments.body:
Design approved and implementation started.

The two read-only design reviews confirmed the one-dashboard approach and tightened the implementation contract:

- source generator and generated artifact are authoritative; Grafana UI edits are not a reverse-sync path;
- both `metadata.name` and `networking/rfc6035-2otel.json` are stable identity;
- the tab title is `Raw Reports`, matching `dtab=Raw-Reports`;
- one-way delay uses a selection-aware hidden variable and row-level conditional rendering;
- exact report/handset summaries use Loki, with event and sender as pipeline filters;
- every Prometheus/Loki query is wired through its datasource variable;
- quality links retain site/sender labels and have a selection-based fallback;
- alerts use stable numeric panel IDs, App Platform resources, a dedicated runtime-resolved folder, scoped prune, and semantic read-back;
- GitSync verification compares the live source path, manager, folder, and pushed Git blob SHA;
- recording rules remain intentionally absent because current volume/cardinality are tiny and selected-range calculations cannot be replaced faithfully by fixed windows.

Current live prerequisites: m7kni is online on Grafana 13.2.0-31629364673; `grafanacloud-prom`, `grafanacloud-logs`, and the GitSync-managed `networking` folder are confirmed. The dedicated alert folder and CI Grafana variables/secret remain to be proven during the publication lane.

Implementation is following the ignored local plan `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-13-operational-dashboard-v2.md`; this issue remains the durable record.
